`cxx/leanrs_apply_arm64.S`): applying an `r × k` matrix over GF(2^8) to `k`
input shards with split-nibble table lookups.

This file proves what the routine leaves in memory in terms of the vector
operations it executes (`accV`): three nested loops (64-byte blocks, output
rows two at a time then one, inputs). `ReedSolomon/Arm64/ApplySpec.lean`
connects that to field arithmetic.
-/
